      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a very decisive take for a backgrounder. If I'm going to include the claim that these concerns are \"largely a political maneuver,\" I need to be able to defend why. \n\nCan you get specific? When opponents talk about the inflationary impact of injecting massive amounts of liquidity into the consumer market, or the long-term impact on the national deficit, are those also just \"smokescreens\"? I need to know if there is any empirical economic basis to those specific fears, or if they are indeed just being used to protect the status quo.",
